"],["arc","דֵ֖ךְ",null,"H1791","APdxms"],["arc","בִּירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם",null,"H3390","AR/Np","b"],["arc","וּרְע֥וּת",null,"H7470","AC/Ncfsc","c"],["arc","מַלְכָּ֛א",null,"H4430","ANcmsd/Td"],["arc","עַל",null,"H5922","AR"],["arc","דְּנָ֖ה",null,"H1836","APdxcs"],["arc","יִשְׁלַ֥ח",null,"H7972","AVqi3ms"],["arc","עֲלֶֽינָא",null,"H5922","AR/Sp1cp"]]},"gl":{"H5013":"to prophesy","H2292":"Haggai","H5029":"prophet","H2148":"Zechariah","H1247":"son","H5714":"Iddo","H5922":"since","H3062":"Jew","H1768":"that","H3061":"Judah","H3390":"Jerusalem","H8036":"name","H426":"god","H3479":"Israel","H116":"then","H6966":"rise","H2217":"Zerubbabel","H7598":"Shealtiel","H3443":"Jeshua","H3136":"Jozadak","H8271":"to loose","H1124":"to build","H1005":"house","H5974":"with","H5583":"to support","H2166":"time","H858":"to come","H8674":"Tattenai","H6347":"governor","H5675":"beyond","H5103":"River","H8370":"Shethar-bozenai","H3675":"associate","H3652":"thus","H560":"to say","H4479":"who?","H7761":"make","H2942":"command","H1836":"this","H846":"wall","H3635":"to complete","H3660":"thus","H581":"they","H1400":"man","H1147":"building","H5870":"eye","H1934":"to be","H7868":"be gray","H3809":"not","H989":"to cease","H1994":"they","H5705":"till","H2941":"account","H1868":"Darius","H1946":"to go","H8421":"return","H5407":"document","H6573":"copy","H104":"letter","H7972":"to send","H671":"governors","H4430":"king","H6600":"edict","H3790":"to write","H1459":"midst","H8001":"peace","H3606":"all","H3046":"to know","H236":"to go","H4083":"province","H7229":"great","H1932":"he/she/it","H69":"stone","H1560":"great","H636":"wood","H3797":"wall","H5673":"service","H1791":"this","H629":"diligently","H5648":"to make","H6744":"to prosper","H3028":"hand","H7593":"to ask","H479":"these","H638":"also","H7217":"head","H586":"we","H5649":"servant/slave","H8065":"heaven","H772":"soil","H6928":"previously","H8140":"year","H7690":"greatly","H3861":"except","H4481":"from","H7265":"to enrage","H2":"father","H3052":"to give","H5020":"Nebuchadnezzar","H895":"Babylon","H3679":"Chaldean","H5642":"to hide","H5972":"people","H1541":"to reveal","H1297":"nevertheless","H2298":"one","H3567":"Cyrus","H3984":"utensil","H1722":"gold","H3702":"silver","H5312":"to go out","H1965":"temple","H2987":"to bring","H8340":"Sheshbazzar","H412":"these","H5376":"to lift","H5182":"to descend","H870":"place","H787":"foundation","H3705":"now","H8000":"be complete","H2006":"if","H2869":"fine","H1240":"to enquire","H1596":"treasure","H8536":"there","H383":"there is","H7470":"pleasure"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Addo was grand-father of the prophet, whose writings are extant. (Calmet) — Both prophesied in the second year of Darius. (Menochius)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Them. Aggeus had rebuked the people for building houses for themselves, while they neglected the temple. The work was hereupon resumed without any fresh order from the king; as the edicts of the usurper, Oropastes, were considered as null, and the Jews only answer the governor, that they had been authorized by Cyrus, ver. 13, 17. Josephus, and 3 Esdras iii., and iv. 47., assert that Darius had given leave. (Calmet) (Menochius)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","River, over all Syria, &c. This man had not been bribed, but acted with great moderation, and in compliance with his duty. (Calmet) — Counsel. Chaldean, “order….to make up this wall.”"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","In. Septuagint, “Then I (or they; eipon. The Syriac and Arabic declare for the latter) said thus to them: What,” &c. — We gave. Chaldean, “what are the names?” (Haydock) — It seems Thathanai asked this question, ver. 10. The Jews might give in the names of Zorobabel, Josue, Aggeus, &c. (Calmet)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Ancients. Septuagint, “captivity of Juda.” (Haydock) — Divine Providence favoured the undertaking. (Delrio adag. 216.) (Menochius) (Psalm xxxii. 18.) — His eye sometimes threatens ruin, Amos ix. 8. (Calmet) — God did both on this occasion. (Worthington) — Hinder. Chaldean, “cause them to leave off, till the matter came to Darius, (Haydock) and his decision was brought back;” (Calmet) or Protestants, “and then they returned answer by letter concerning this matter.” Septuagint, “and they did not molest them, till the sentence should be brought to (or from) Darius; and then it (word) was sent to the tax-gatherer, concerning this affair.“"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Unpolished. Protestants, “great.” (Haydock) — Hebrew, “to be rolled.” See Vitruv. x. 6. Septuagint, “choice stones.” Kimchi, &c., “marble.” (Calmet) — 3 Esdras, “polished and precious stones.” (Haydock) — Yet the Vulgate seems more conformable to chap. vi. 4., and Aggeus ii. 2. (Menochius) (Ribera) — Walls, every fourth course, 3 Kings vi. 36. (Calmet)"],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Built. It did not appear that this edict had been revoked; (Calmet) nor could it be changed, if it had been passed by the advice of the Lord. (Haydock)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Governor. Septuagint, “over the treasury.”"],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","In building, being pretty far advanced, though for some time past it had been at a stand. (Haydock) — It is not probable that Zorobabel said this, but the author of the letter added it, as he supposed the Jews continued to do some little. (Calmet) — He desired to favour their cause, yet so as not to irritate the Samaritans. (Menochius)"],["haydock",17,null,"haydock","Library. Septuagint, “treasury-house.” Arabic, “for the archives.” It is called “the house of books,” chap. vi. 1. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}